{
  "name": "Siberys Powder (Horn)",
  "type": "consumable",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p><strong>Activate</strong> <span class=\"pf2-icon\">1</span> Interact</p>\n<p>Siberys powder is a volatile and explosive alchemical substance commonly used in the production of wand munitions. Siberys powder becomes inert and useless when wet and must be kept in a sealed, water-tight container.</p>\n<p>A horn contains 500 doses worth of siberys powder. A horn can be detonated by leaving a small trail of siberys powder and then lighting it. Each 5-foot square requires one dose of siberys powder to create a trail through. As long as the horn is mostly full (at least 400 doses remaining) it can be detonated to deal [[/r 1d6[fire]]] damage in a @Template[type:burst|distance:5] (@Check[type:reflex|dc:16|basic:true|name:Siberys Powder Detonation] save). It takes 1 round per 15 feet of powder trail laid down for a horn to detonate after the trail is lit. If multiple horns detonate simultaneously, it can increase the area of the explosion, but the damage in overlapping areas doesn't increase.</p>"
    },
    "source": {
      "value": "Pathfinder's Guide to Eberron"
    },
